 ## Operating characteristics
-Rendering speed reaches 900+ FPS with high quality [S1, unofficial]. Training time drastically shortens or bypasses the per-scene gradient descent loop [S1, unofficial]. Pruning reduces memory usage compared to dense SfM-initialized Gaussians [S2, unofficial]. Strengths include high-quality initialization, robustness to topological pitfalls of SfM, and high rendering speed [S1, S2, unofficial]. Limitations include the upfront computational cost of NeRF training [S1, unofficial]. Not given in the sources for specific memory complexity formulas.
