 ## Background
-RadSplat was introduced to improve 3DGS initialization by replacing raw SfM point clouds with NeRF-derived dense point clouds [S1, S2, unofficial]. It addresses the noise and topological errors inherent in SfM data [S1, unofficial]. The method is cited in surveys on 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization and recent advances in the field [S1, S2, unofficial].
